# DTF tier manifest: rpm-hosted-repodata-precomputed
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + client.dnf (a real Fedora RPM client).
#
# artifact-keeper#4544 (#5067, #5069, #5073): hosted RPM repodata is built in
# the background and served from storage. The oracle publishes two RPMs (the
# second depends on the first), calls `rebuild?wait=true` (read-your-writes
# for CI), checks that the served repomd.xml is the stored revision, runs a
# real `dnf makecache` + `dnf install` through the client, and checks the
# stored bytes equal the on-request render (`repodata_mode: on_request`) of
# the same content. Red on 1.11.9 (the rebuild endpoint does not exist: 404).
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: admin login, uploads and back-to-back metadata
# fetches through one admin user.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.dnf"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
